  "verbalization": "The visible evidence strongly suggests a mechanistic link between the compound [(1S,2S,3R,5S,8R,9R,10R,14S)-2,9,10-triacetyloxy-5-hydroxy-8,12,15,15-tetramethyl-4-methylidene-14-tricyclo[9.3.1.03,8]pentadec-11-enyl] 2-methylbutanoate and Taste receptor type 2 member 31. This compound is identified as a target of multiple peptides, including Sugiol, Cornuside, and Npc158230, all of which are known to interact with the same target. The shared mechanism of action involves the inhibition of a target enzyme, which in this case is Peptide deformylase. This enzyme is critical for the proper processing of peptides, and its inhibition may disrupt the function of Taste receptor type 2 member 31, thereby affecting taste perception. The consistent evidence across three distinct paths supports a unified mechanism, where the compound acts as a modulator of the target enzyme, leading to a downstream effect on the receptor. The presence of multiple targets that ultimately converge on the same receptor suggests a robust and well-defined pathway, reinforcing the hypothesis that the compound exerts its effect through this specific mechanism.",
